WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:29.833


2
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:31.375
<b>In previous verses,</b>

3
00:00:31.375 --> 00:00:35.083
<b>Lord Krishna explained that desire is an enemy</b>

4
00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:40.875
<b>that perpetually dwells in our</b>
<b>senses, mind, and intellect.</b>

5
00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:43.083
<b>In the following verses,</b>

6
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:47.750
<b>Krishna will reveal how to confront this enemy.</b>

7
00:00:48.416 --> 00:00:52.666


8
00:00:52.666 --> 00:01:00.250
<b>Desire resides in three places: our</b>
<b>senses, our mind, and our intellect.</b>

9
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:07.041
<b>To control this enemy, we must strike </b>
<b>at all three locations.</b>

10
00:01:07.041 --> 00:01:11.625
<b>Among these, the senses </b>
<b>can be experienced directly,</b>

11
00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:17.875
<b>making them easier to control compared </b>
<b>to the mind and intellect.</b>

12
00:01:17.875 --> 00:01:23.833
<b>Since mind and intellect are abstract, </b>
<b>they're more challenging to master.</b>

13
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:30.666
<b>This is why Krishna suggests </b>
<b>beginning with sensory control.</b>

14
00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:34.500
<b>By keeping our senses away</b>
<b>from harmful influences</b>

15
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.875
<b>and directing them towards positive pursuits</b>

16
00:01:37.875 --> 00:01:40.458
<b>control over them becomes possible</b>

17
00:01:40.458 --> 00:01:49.125
<b>Without such control, the senses risk falling </b>
<b>back under the influence of desire.</b>

18
00:01:49.125 --> 00:01:51.416
<b>But how do we achieve this?</b>

19
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:58.875
<b>Let's understand through the example </b>
<b>of someone trying to lose weight.</b>

20
00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:06.041
<b>The simple approach would be </b>
<b>to avoid certain foods, like sweets,</b>

21
00:02:06.041 --> 00:02:09.666
<b>but doing this immediately proves difficult.</b>

22
00:02:09.666 --> 00:02:16.583
<b>Therefore, such a person is advised to </b>
<b>continue eating what they like</b>

23
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:20.416
<b>but gradually reduce the portions.</b>

24
00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:24.541
<b>This represents planned moderation.</b>

25
00:02:24.541 --> 00:02:30.958
<b>Through such restraint, the person's </b>
<b>cravings gradually diminish,</b>

26
00:02:30.958 --> 00:02:34.958
<b>and these desires begin to </b>
<b>fade from the mind as well.</b>

27
00:02:34.958 --> 00:02:36.500
<b>Another understanding is this</b>

28
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.458
<b>that we should use our senses in such a way</b>

29
00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:43.333
<b>that any such temptations or harmful things </b>
<b>should never be given the opportunity </b>

30
00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:47.333
<b>to be seen, heard, or experienced.</b>

31
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.958
<b>that could awaken desire.</b>

32
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:55.708
<b>For instance, staying away from sensual</b>
<b>or obscene scenes and films,</b>

33
00:02:55.708 --> 00:03:01.125
<b>as these can reawaken dormant physical desires.</b>

34
00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:03.416
<b>Some foolish people believe</b>

35
00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:09.416
<b>we should enjoy all sensory </b>
<b>pleasures available in creation,</b>

36
00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:13.125
<b>arguing that otherwise, </b>
<b>this body and life are worthless.</b>

37
00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.666
<b>If this were true,</b>

38
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:18.708
<b>then both sweets and poison are part of creation,</b>

39
00:03:18.708 --> 00:03:22.416
<b>yet we avoid poison but not sweets.</b>

40
00:03:22.416 --> 00:03:28.916
<b>This is because we know poison</b>
<b>directly harms the body.</b>

41
00:03:28.916 --> 00:03:30.708
<b>This reflects materialistic thinking –</b>

42
00:03:30.708 --> 00:03:34.708
<b>we shy away from what harms the body</b>

43
00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:40.791
<b>but aren't cautious about </b>
<b>what damages the mind.</b>

44
00:03:40.791 --> 00:03:48.333
<b>If senses remain uncontrolled </b>
<b>and freely consume spiritual poison,</b>

45
00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:54.458
<b>eventually both knowledge and </b>
<b>spiritual understanding will be destroyed.</b>

46
00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:58.166
<b>Krishna identifies desire as a great symbol of sin.</b>

47
00:03:58.166 --> 00:03:59.416
<b>Why?</b>

48
00:03:59.416 --> 00:04:02.083
<b>Because first, a person falls into desire,</b>

49
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:06.083
<b>and then it drives them to sin.</b>

50
00:04:06.083 --> 00:04:09.583
<b>Just as a white flag symbolizes peace,</b>

51
00:04:09.583 --> 00:04:12.625
<b>similarly desire symbolizes sin.</b>

52
00:04:12.625 --> 00:04:16.041
<b>If you see someone surrounded by desire,</b>

53
00:04:16.041 --> 00:04:21.041
<b>be certain they're engaged in </b>
<b>some form of wrongdoing.</b>

54
00:04:21.041 --> 00:04:23.500
<b>And remember this:</b>

55
00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.416
<b>the definition of sin doesn't </b>
<b>depend on people's opinions.</b>

56
00:04:27.416 --> 00:04:34.250
<b>Just because most people don't consider </b>
<b>something sinful doesn't make it pure.</b>

57
00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.541
<b>A group of thieves cannot determine legal rules.</b>

58
00:04:38.541 --> 00:04:43.708
<b>There are specific institutions to </b>
<b>create and enforce these rules,</b>

59
00:04:43.708 --> 00:04:46.083
<b>and special books containing these laws.</b>

60
00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:52.791
<b>Similarly, right and wrong cannot </b>
<b>be determined by people's collective wishes.</b>

61
00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:57.125
<b>These guidelines are clearly</b>
<b>stated in the scriptures.</b>

62
00:04:57.125 --> 00:05:03.125
<b>Any violation of these </b>
<b>directives is spiritually harmful.</b>

63
00:05:03.125 --> 00:05:06.875
<b>And ultimately, according to spiritual laws,</b>

64
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:10.666
<b>one must face the consequences of such actions.</b>

65
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:15.500


66
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.333
<b>Your senses</b>

67
00:05:18.333 --> 00:05:26.958
<b>are gateways through which various </b>
<b>influences enter your mind</b>

68
00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:31.958
<b>and shape your desires as well.</b>

69
00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:36.041
<b>If these gates are left unguarded,</b>

70
00:05:36.041 --> 00:05:41.916
<b>all influences will flow in unchecked,</b>

71
00:05:41.916 --> 00:05:48.666
<b>awakening numerous emotions and desires</b>

72
00:05:48.666 --> 00:05:55.541
<b>that will lead you astray from </b>
<b>your goals and values.</b>

73
00:05:55.541 --> 00:05:57.250
<b>This is why</b>

74
00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:05.291
<b>it's crucial to maintain control over these </b>
<b>sensory gateways of your mind's dwelling.</b>

75
00:06:05.291 --> 00:06:15.083
<b>Consider, for instance, </b>
<b>someone who wishes to lose weight.</b>

76
00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:23.625
<b>If this person continues to indulge in </b>
<b>everything that tempts them,</b>

77
00:06:23.625 --> 00:06:29.500
<b>then weight loss becomes nearly impossible.</b>

78
00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.041
<b>However,</b>

79
00:06:31.041 --> 00:06:34.041
<b>by regulating their diet—</b>

80
00:06:34.041 --> 00:06:36.083
<b>choosing healthy foods,</b>

81
00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:38.416
<b>reducing portions,</b>

82
00:06:38.416 --> 00:06:41.666
<b>avoiding harmful dishes—</b>

83
00:06:41.666 --> 00:06:46.750
<b>they can gradually diminish their cravings</b>

84
00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:52.166
<b>and surely achieve their goal.</b>

85
00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:57.750
<b>This principle applies to all our senses.</b>

86
00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:05.000
<b>When we indulge our senses without restraint—</b>

87
00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:11.375
<b>be it through stimulating visuals, unhealthy food,</b>

88
00:07:11.375 --> 00:07:14.875
<b>or other temptations—</b>

89
00:07:14.875 --> 00:07:21.083
<b>we intensify our desires to such an extent</b>

90
00:07:21.083 --> 00:07:26.041
<b>that controlling them becomes </b>
<b>increasingly difficult with time.</b>

91
00:07:26.041 --> 00:07:31.166
<b>But if we mindfully choose</b>

92
00:07:31.166 --> 00:07:33.083
<b>what we see,</b>

93
00:07:33.083 --> 00:07:34.250
<b>what we hear,</b>

94
00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:35.541
<b>and what we taste,</b>

95
00:07:35.541 --> 00:07:43.000
<b>we can positively guide our mind's tendencies.</b>

96
00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.708
<b>For example,</b>

97
00:07:44.708 --> 00:07:50.041
<b>if you distance yourself from </b>
<b>provocative scenes or films,</b>

98
00:07:50.041 --> 00:07:53.791
<b>physical desires will remain dormant.</b>

99
00:07:53.791 --> 00:07:55.291
<b>Yet,</b>

100
00:07:55.291 --> 00:08:01.416
<b>keeping the senses completely inactive</b>
<b>isn't always possible or desirable.</b>

101
00:08:01.416 --> 00:08:05.458
<b>Instead, channel them into worthy pursuits.</b>

102
00:08:05.458 --> 00:08:07.708
<b>There are numerous ways:</b>

103
00:08:07.708 --> 00:08:09.583
<b>reading enriching books,</b>

104
00:08:09.583 --> 00:08:11.958
<b>engaging in meaningful conversations,</b>

105
00:08:11.958 --> 00:08:16.166
<b>watching educational films, </b>
<b>practicing meditation.</b>

106
00:08:16.166 --> 00:08:26.958
<b>By mastering our senses and consequently </b>
<b>our desires, we develop a disciplined life.</b>

107
00:08:26.958 --> 00:08:33.625
<b>And such a disciplined life leads </b>
<b>us toward our worthy goals.</b>

108
00:08:34.125 --> 00:08:38.541


109
00:08:38.541 --> 00:08:41.458
<b>In today's modern world,</b>

110
00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:45.041
<b>a culture of "excess" has become prevalent,</b>

111
00:08:45.041 --> 00:08:51.250
<b>where the motto seems to be 'more is better.'</b>

112
00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:54.666
<b>Additionally, many businesses </b>
<b>now offer instant gratification,</b>

113
00:08:54.666 --> 00:09:03.041
<b>delivering whatever you desire </b>
<b>at the click of a button.</b>

114
00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:05.791
<b>In such times, within the family,</b>

115
00:09:05.791 --> 00:09:13.041
<b>establishing values like self-control and </b>
<b>moderation has become increasingly challenging.</b>

116
00:09:13.041 --> 00:09:16.583
<b>You must have heard the saying,</b>

117
00:09:16.583 --> 00:09:27.583
<b>'What's popular isn't necessarily right, </b>
<b>and what's right isn't necessarily popular.'</b>

118
00:09:27.583 --> 00:09:32.125
<b>This statement holds profound </b>
<b>truth in today's times.</b>

119
00:09:32.125 --> 00:09:40.166
<b>Just because a lifestyle or behavior is </b>
<b>widespread doesn't mean it's beneficial.</b>

120
00:09:40.166 --> 00:09:41.916
<b>For instance,</b>

121
00:09:41.916 --> 00:09:50.125
<b>spending hours watching entertainment </b>
<b>programs on television is quite popular,</b>

122
00:09:50.125 --> 00:09:52.458
<b>but is it beneficial?</b>

123
00:09:52.458 --> 00:09:58.250
<b>Being constantly engaged with </b>
<b>our phones is common,</b>

124
00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.916
<b>but is it worthwhile?</b>

125
00:10:00.916 --> 00:10:05.250
<b>We often lose ourselves in the </b>
<b>colorful world of these devices,</b>

126
00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.875
<b>forgetting that it's merely an illusion.</b>

127
00:10:09.875 --> 00:10:12.291
<b>Our real world lies here—</b>

128
00:10:12.291 --> 00:10:15.875
<b>with our family members, </b>
<b>our bonds with them,</b>

129
00:10:15.875 --> 00:10:17.375
<b> our connections.</b>

130
00:10:17.375 --> 00:10:21.958
<b>This is what truly gives meaning to life.</b>

131
00:10:21.958 --> 00:10:28.791
<b>Families that prioritize strong values and </b>
<b>mutual love will naturally display discipline,</b>

132
00:10:28.791 --> 00:10:37.125
<b>and this is the culture all families </b>
<b>should strive to develop.</b>

133
00:10:37.125 --> 00:10:39.666
<b>This doesn't mean</b>

134
00:10:39.666 --> 00:10:47.583
<b>completely banning entertainment </b>
<b>or other enjoyable activities,</b>

135
00:10:47.583 --> 00:10:48.458
<b>but</b>

136
00:10:48.458 --> 00:10:53.416
<b>maintaining moderation and a </b>
<b>balanced perspective is crucial.</b>

137
00:10:53.416 --> 00:10:59.625
<b>We must consider how family</b>
<b>members spend their time</b>

138
00:10:59.625 --> 00:11:05.291
<b>and its impact on family relationships.</b>

139
00:11:05.291 --> 00:11:06.500
<b>However,</b>

140
00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.416
<b>such change becomes possible</b>

141
00:11:09.416 --> 00:11:15.375
<b>only when family elders set an </b>
<b>example of such moderate living.</b>

142
00:11:15.375 --> 00:11:26.291
<b>When elders choose activities based on their</b>
<b>positive impact rather than their popularity,</b>

143
00:11:26.291 --> 00:11:33.958
<b>it can inspire the youth and children in the family.</b>

144
00:11:33.958 --> 00:11:38.500
<b>Seeing this behavior in elders, </b>
<b>children will understand</b>

145
00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.083
<b>that control doesn't mean complete restriction,</b>

146
00:11:42.083 --> 00:11:47.416
<b>but rather making right choices </b>
<b>in right measures.</b>

147
00:11:47.416 --> 00:11:50.708
<b>Develop family values</b>

148
00:11:50.708 --> 00:11:56.083
<b>where members not only understand the </b>
<b>importance of moderation and balance</b>

149
00:11:56.083 --> 00:12:01.000
<b>but embrace it wholeheartedly.</b>

150
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:04.125
<b>Learn and teach how to make right choices,</b>

151
00:12:04.125 --> 00:12:08.416
<b>regardless of their popularity.</b>

152
00:12:08.416 --> 00:12:09.958
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

153
00:12:10.458 --> 00:12:14.750


154
00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:19.958
<b>In the fiercely competitive environment </b>
<b>of modern workplaces,</b>

155
00:12:19.958 --> 00:12:28.458
<b>the temptation to take shortcuts or </b>
<b>engage in unethical behavior can be strong.</b>

156
00:12:28.458 --> 00:12:36.958
<b>These temptations are similar to the </b>
<b>external influences affecting our senses.</b>

157
00:12:36.958 --> 00:12:46.958
<b>Just as uncontrolled senses can increase </b>
<b>harmful desires and cause damage,</b>

158
00:12:46.958 --> 00:12:51.958
<b>these temptations can be </b>
<b>destructive to professional life.</b>

159
00:12:51.958 --> 00:13:00.375
<b>Just as a strong house requires </b>
<b>a deep and solid foundation,</b>

160
00:13:00.375 --> 00:13:02.166
<b>professional life,</b>

161
00:13:02.166 --> 00:13:09.500
<b>professional life, if not built on the solid ground </b>
<b>of integrity, discipline, and self-control,</b>

162
00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:13.625
<b>may weaken over time.</b>

163
00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:15.000
<b>In professional life,</b>

164
00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:17.291
<b>discipline means</b>

165
00:13:17.291 --> 00:13:21.416
<b>respecting others' time and your own,</b>

166
00:13:21.416 --> 00:13:26.083
<b>while maintaining decorum in every interaction.</b>

167
00:13:26.083 --> 00:13:34.916
<b>Integrity means consistently maintaining </b>
<b>the quality of your work with honesty.</b>

168
00:13:34.916 --> 00:13:40.625
<b>It means dealing fairly and </b>
<b>truthfully with everyone,</b>

169
00:13:40.625 --> 00:13:45.625
<b>and most importantly,</b>

170
00:13:45.625 --> 00:13:53.125
<b>standing firm in your values whether </b>
<b>someone is watching or not, </b>

171
00:13:53.125 --> 00:13:59.125
<b>whether anyone appreciates it or not.</b>

172
00:13:59.125 --> 00:14:02.500
<b>The third pillar, self-control,</b>

173
00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:10.125
<b>becomes crucial when faced </b>
<b>with various temptations.</b>

174
00:14:10.125 --> 00:14:19.458
<b>These might include the desire </b>
<b>to criticize others for promotion,</b>

175
00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:23.666
<b>the lure of unethical practices, and </b>

176
00:14:23.666 --> 00:14:33.333
<b>even physical attraction toward colleagues—</b>
<b>which is also a form of mental temptation.</b>

177
00:14:33.333 --> 00:14:38.750
<b>If self-control breaks in such situations,</b>

178
00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:43.916
<b>the consequences can be severely damaging.</b>

179
00:14:43.916 --> 00:14:45.250
<b>Moreover,</b>

180
00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:49.166
<b>it's essential for any organization</b>

181
00:14:49.166 --> 00:14:56.041
<b>to not only explain the importance of </b>
<b>these three values to its employees</b>

182
00:14:56.041 --> 00:14:59.875
<b>but to reinforce them regularly.</b>

183
00:14:59.875 --> 00:15:01.541
<b>Remember,</b>

184
00:15:01.541 --> 00:15:08.208
<b>following these three values—</b>
<b>discipline, integrity, and self-control—</b>

185
00:15:08.208 --> 00:15:13.791
<b>is as important for those in leadership positions</b>

186
00:15:13.791 --> 00:15:18.333
<b>as it is for those working under them.</b>

187
00:15:18.333 --> 00:15:23.041
<b>Only when senior officers embody these values</b>

188
00:15:23.041 --> 00:15:27.916
<b>will their importance spread</b>
<b>throughout the organization.</b>

189
00:15:27.916 --> 00:15:30.750
<b>And yes, these three qualities</b>

190
00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:38.416
<b>are equally valuable not just in professional life, </b>
<b>but in personal life as well.</b>

191
00:15:38.416 --> 00:15:41.000
<b>Always adhere to them.</b>

